% Ruby HTTP client host attribution — Tier FX. Replaces
% internal/linker/ruby_http_hosts.go's ResolveRubyHTTPHosts (Tier L).
%
% Unlike go_http_hosts.dl, this is pure pass-through — see
% internal/factpipe/hub_ruby_http_hosts.go's doc comment for why: the
% cross-file registry fold IS a genuine whole-service fixpoint (sticky
% conflict on a host-method name registered with two different env vars,
% one L.1 "delegate" hop), but resolveHostExpr's per-call-site trace never
% opens a second file, and the path-template text synthesis it depends on
% (interpolation-by-interpolation string building, parameter-hole
% substitution) has no join-shaped equivalent — no `.dl` builtin does
% string concatenation. The hub already resolved the winning (env, path)
% pair per node before asserting one fact per outcome; there is nothing
% left here to join. (Same precedent as gorm_tables.dl.)

ruby_host_env_rel(NodeID, Env, Raw) :- ruby_host_env(NodeID, Env, Raw).
ruby_host_path_rel(NodeID, Path) :- ruby_host_path(NodeID, Path).
